<title>USA: Albertson's buys Utah store among 70 for '96.</title>
<headline>Albertson's buys Utah store among 70 for '96.</headline>
<dateline>BOISE, Idaho 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Albertson's Inc said on Thursday that it has bought a 26,200-square-foot food and drug store in Riverton, Utah, from Gorman Foods Inc as part of its plans to open 70 stores this year.</p>
<p>The company currently operates 801 stores and said 43 of the 70 stores are now open.</p>
<p>Albertson's said it would expand the newly acquired Utah store, which is in a suburb of Salt Lake City.</p>
</text>
